Uploads hardening (Module 7) -- apply together with java/com/aria/utils/UploadGuard.java.

Why: /uploads/** is permit-all and served from the application's own origin. Both upload
endpoints below store ANY file type under the client's file name, so an uploaded .html / .svg runs
as the app (stored XSS) for whoever opens the link. The PICO modules route selfies (Module 1),
expense receipts (Module 4) and profile photos (Module 7) through these endpoints.

